From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:55:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: name the T8132 PMP scratch
 registers to the firmware

T8132 sent no PMP_CTRL_SET because its PMP scratch registers were not
known. macOS 26B123 on the J604 sends it at every firmware start, and
the firmware prints what it got: "PMP clock[scratch 0x3803d0ce0, Int
0x0(bit 0), size 8], bandwidth[scratch 0x382824000, Int 0x0(bit 0),
size 8]", followed by "Requested Vmin (320MHz) to PMP". Both registers
are already mapped 1:1 for the firmware (the PMGR and PMP bandwidth
scratch windows), so the firmware can then ask the PMP for the clock
and bandwidth its pipeline needs, as it does on macOS.

Pass those values for T8132. The pmp_ctrl module parameter, on by
default, can hold the command back on any SoC.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c  | 11 ++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
index 186135313b..8ca5e6c05a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
@@ -1272,8 +1272,10 @@ static const struct isp_mmio_window apple_isp_fw_mmio_t8132[] = {
 /*
  * T8132 runs T6040's coprocessor and firmware interface, booted the same
  * way. Its two AMCCs (ADT mcc amcc_aperture_count) give two broadcast-clear
- * windows, passed one per AMCC without padding slots. No PMP_CTRL_SET is
- * sent: T8132's PMP scratch offsets are not established. Its firmware
+ * windows, passed one per AMCC without padding slots. PMP_CTRL_SET names
+ * the PMP clock and bandwidth scratch registers macOS 26B123 passes on the
+ * J604 (its firmware prints them: clock 0x3803d0ce0, bandwidth 0x382824000,
+ * base 0, bit 0, size 8). Its firmware
  * starts again from its data segment as loaded once the coprocessor was
  * quiesced before the power-down, so the ISP is powered only while the
  * camera is in use.
@@ -1288,6 +1290,15 @@ static const struct apple_isp_hw apple_isp_hw_t8132 = {
 	.dsid_clr_base1 = 0x2221d4000,
 	.dsid_clr_range0 = 0x2fc,
 
+	.clock_scratch = 0x3803d0ce0,
+	.clock_base = 0x0,
+	.clock_bit = 0x0,
+	.clock_size = 0x8,
+	.bandwidth_scratch = 0x382824000,
+	.bandwidth_base = 0x0,
+	.bandwidth_bit = 0x0,
+	.bandwidth_size = 0x8,
+
 	.mbox_irq_enable = ISP_MBOX_IRQ_ENABLE_T6031,
 	.mbox_irq_route_t8132 = ISP_MBOX_IRQ_ROUTE_T8132,
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c
index 89b11f3b04..bbf581509a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c
@@ -55,6 +55,15 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(core_park,
  * Write the ISP DART setup and the word before it at each power-up as
  * macOS does where they are known (T8132). Read at each power-up.
  */
+/*
+ * Name the PMP clock and bandwidth scratch registers to the firmware
+ * (PMP_CTRL_SET) where they are known. Read when the firmware starts.
+ */
+static bool pmp_ctrl = true;
+module_param(pmp_ctrl, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(pmp_ctrl,
+		 "Send PMP_CTRL_SET where the PMP scratch registers are known (default: on)");
+
 static bool macos_dart_setup = true;
 module_param(macos_dart_setup, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(macos_dart_setup,
@@ -1215,7 +1224,7 @@ static int isp_start_command_processor(struct apple_isp *isp)
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	if (isp->hw->clock_scratch) {
+	if (isp->hw->clock_scratch && READ_ONCE(pmp_ctrl)) {
 		err = isp_cmd_pmp_ctrl_set(
 			isp, isp->hw->clock_scratch, isp->hw->clock_base,
 			isp->hw->clock_bit, isp->hw->clock_size,
-- 
2.43.0

